# Design tokens

Token sources generate the values used by components, CSS, docs, Penpot, Figma, and Flutter.

## Source layers

All paths below are relative to `packages/tokens/`.

<DocsTable columns={sourceColumns} rows={sourceRows} minWidth="var(--ds-sizing-2xl)" />

Add reusable values to shared sources and role-based names to the semantic layer.

## Generate outputs

```sh
npm run tokens
```

Run `npm run tokens:web` for CSS and `npm run tokens:design-tools` for Penpot, Figma, and Flutter exports.

<DocsTable columns={outputColumns} rows={outputRows} minWidth="var(--ds-sizing-2xl)" />

## Use tokens

Import the core styles once at the application root:

```css
@import '@aesir/css/aesir-global.css';
@import '@aesir/css/aesir-motion.css';
```

Add `aesir-typography.css` only when the application should use Aesir's semantic HTML defaults.

Use semantic tokens for roles and foundation tokens for layout values:

```css
.panel {
	padding: var(--ds-spacing-4);
	border: var(--ds-spacing-px) solid var(--ds-border);
	border-radius: var(--ds-radius-lg);
	background: var(--ds-surface);
	color: var(--ds-foreground);
}
```

## Change a token

1. Edit the appropriate source file.
2. Run `npm run tokens`.
3. Review light and dark themes.
4. Commit the source and generated outputs together.

The design-tool exports separate shared tokens from three independent choices: `mode` (Light or Dark), `theme` (Default, Mist, Protanopia / deuteranopia, or Tritanopia), and `accent` (a color). In Penpot, enable `AESIR/global` and `AESIR/semantic`, then select one option in each group.

In Figma, create collections named `AESIR Global`, `AESIR Mode`, `AESIR Semantic`, `AESIR Theme`, and `AESIR Accent`. Import each file into its matching collection; import all files in `mode`, `theme`, and `accent` as modes of their respective collections. Import Mode before Semantic and Theme, and Theme before Accent, so cross-collection aliases can resolve. Apply colors from `AESIR Theme` and `AESIR Accent` to designs; `AESIR Semantic` is the unmodified reference layer.

